<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coolgardie</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Coolgardie is a town in the Goldfields region of Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>. Gold was found there in 1892 by Arthur Bayley and William Ford, starting a rush that briefly made it the third-largest town in the colony. Its importance faded after the richer discoveries at nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalgoorlie">Kalgoorlie</a>, and it is now a small town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coolgardie.jpg" alt="Coolgardie" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nachoman-au · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coolgardie_Town_Hall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
